Filed by langertha-adr-auditor while recording ADR 0018 (provider wire-spelling normalization). Prose-only work is done; this is the code half.

State at HEAD 07f6d68:

  lib/Langertha/Response.pm:415-423  (karr k125, commit 196a274)
    if ( !exists $params->{cached_tokens} && ref( $params->{usage} ) eq "HASH" ) {
      my $usage = $params->{usage};
      my $ptd   = $usage->{prompt_tokens_details};
      if ( ref($ptd) eq "HASH" && defined $ptd->{cached_tokens} ) { ... }
      elsif ( defined $usage->{cache_read_input_tokens} )         { ... }
    }

Two provider wire spellings of a usage quantity are hand-parsed in Response::BUILDARGS.
Forty lines further down (Response.pm:463-467) the SAME BUILDARGS delegates the rest of the
usage block to the value object: Langertha::Usage->from_hash( $params->{usage} ) -- and
from_hash (Usage.pm:61-82) is already the multi-spelling inbound door, knowing three
families for input (input_tokens / prompt_tokens / prompt_eval_count) and three for output
(output_tokens / completion_tokens / eval_count).

So the same method both delegates usage parsing to the value object and hand-parses two
usage spellings itself. Under ADR 0001 ("the value object owns inbound parsing"), ADR 0017
(Moment->from_wire is the lenient inbound door, "the parse lives in the value object, not
in the engine") and ADR 0018 home 1, the cache-read spellings belong on Langertha::Usage.

Root cause is placement, not carelessness: cached_tokens is modeled as a Response attribute
(Response.pm:358) rather than on Langertha::Usage, so k125 had nowhere else to put the
spellings. Engine::AKI (AKI.pm:302) passes cached_tokens explicitly for the same reason.

Suggested shape (needs a decision, NOT a blind move):
1. Add cached_tokens (or a cache read/write pair) to Langertha::Usage, parsed in from_hash
   from both usage.prompt_tokens_details.cached_tokens and usage.cache_read_input_tokens.
2. Response::BUILDARGS lifts the PARSED value off the Usage object, not off the raw hash --
   Response keeps its attribute (public API, do not break it) and loses the wire knowledge.
3. Decide what happens to Anthropic cache_creation_input_tokens (a write count, deliberately
   not folded into cached_tokens today) -- a sibling attribute or nothing.
4. Keep the precedence rules k125 established: an explicit cached_tokens parameter wins; the
   OpenAI nesting wins over the Anthropic flat key when both are present; no autovivification
   of the caller usage hash.

Behavior today is CORRECT and gated (t/91_response_usage.t) -- this is a seam-consistency
item, not a bug. Non-blocking.

Related: ADR 0018 (Future work), ADR 0001, ADR 0017, karr k125.


